A||||4||Leadfoot||Why not an AMC 2.5L||||1||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||06-20-2001||06:00 PM||||I have seen a lot of guys with Dukes talking about beefing up their 4 bangers.  I use to own a blazer with a Duke in it.  Boy was it slow....but torquee.  It was rated at 89 hp, and to get that power you always had to rev the crap outta it.  Anyways, I own a wrangler which also has a 2.5L (150 ci).  It is rated at a about 110 hp at 5500 rpm.  The engine is very reliable and has a chain driven valve train (no more chewed up cam gear).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>What I am wondering is why don't Duke owners look at this engine instead? That is if it is possible.  I am not trying to insult anyone so please no flames.  The Dukes are fine engines....I am just curious why people don't try this avenue.  Although if you go that way, might as well go that extra mile and get that V8.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||06-20-2001||09:22 PM||||I think most most people decide it's not worth the effort, when a V6 swap is relative straightforward (as engine swaps go).  However, it would be nice to have 4-cylinder that would rev past 5,000.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||06-20-2001||11:05 PM||||The early 80's CJ7's used a GM Iron Duck (Duke) this was a RWD engine though, it has different mounting points cast into the block for RWD use. Here is a page with a little on the AMC 150 <A HREF="http://www.off-road.com/jeep/tech/engine/amc150.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.off-road.com/jeep/tech/engine/amc150.html</A> <P>Seems like too much trouble for another 4 banger, I would rather say go witha Q4 or just a 2.8 swap instead||||reg||1
Z||000003||sparks||06-22-2001||12:08 PM||||I've got the AMC MPFI in my '97 Wrangler as well.  The timing gear is fixable in a Duke= Metal Timing gears, BTDT before they stripped.<P>Anyway, why bother, the intake AND exhaust would be on the backside which would make it more difficult to get it put in there.  Like Hank is Here said, go with a Q4 if you want a 4 banger or a V8 or V8 for the effort.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leadfoot||06-22-2001||12:12 PM||||O Right.  Forgot they are both on the same side.  Anyway, I thought that if people want to squeeze blood out of a turnip...why not just get a different type of turnip.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
